<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n30445" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">nātālīcĭus</span></b> , <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">-tĭus</span></b> ,
			a, um, adj.
		1. natalis, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>of</i> or <i>belonging to the
			hour</i> or <i>day of one's birth, birthday,
			natal</i> (class.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">qui haec Chaldaeorum natalicia praedicta
					defendunt,</span>”
				<i>a casting of nativities</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Div. 2, 42, 89</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">sidera,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. ib. 2, 43, 91</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">dapes,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Mart.
					7, 86, 1</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">lardum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Juv.
					11, 84</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">sinciput,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Petr. 136</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Pers. 1, 16</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">dies natalicius,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Vulg.
					Gen. 40, 20</span></i>
			.—Hence, </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>Subst</i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">nātālīcĭ-um</span></b> 
				(<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">-tĭum</span></b> ), ii, n., <i>a birthday present</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">aliquid natalicii titulo tibi mittere,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Censor. de Die Nat. 1</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">nātālīcĭa</span></b> ,
				ae, f. (sc. cena), <i>a
				birthday entertainment</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">hodie non descendit Antonius. Cur? Dat
					nataliciam in hortis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Phil. 2, 6, 15</span></i>
			 (so acc. to Cod Vat.; others natalicia, as n.
			plur.).</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
